window.WIKI_FILES.push({file:"category-buddhist-calendar.md",mtime:1795049113,hash:"c833dab77c9cdfbc8f21daa966e986e7580c16d6f21e254b920b42906e359bb0",text:`---
title: Category:Buddhist calendar
categories: [Practice]
---

Pages about the Theravāda lunar calendar, by which the uposatha days, the rains residence and the great festivals are reckoned.

The year has twelve lunar months of 29 or 30 days, each named after the constellation ({{term|nakkhatta}}) near which the moon is full. The months are grouped into three seasons of four months: the hot season ({{term|gimhāna}}), the rainy season ({{term|vassāna}}) and the cold season ({{term|hemanta}}). In leap years an extra month, the second [[Āsāḷha]], is added so that the calendar keeps pace with the seasons.

## The twelve months

| No. | Pāli | Season | Burmese | Sinhala | Gregorian (about) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [[Citta]] | Hot season | Tagu (တန်ခူး) | Bak | March to April |
| 2 | [[Vesākha]] | Hot season | Kason (ကဆုန်) | Vesak | April to May |
| 3 | [[Jeṭṭha]] | Hot season | Nayon (နယုန်) | Poson | May to June |
| 4 | [[Āsāḷha]] | Hot season | Waso (ဝါဆို) | Esala | June to July |
| 5 | [[Sāvaṇa]] | Rainy season | Wagaung (ဝါခေါင်) | Nikini | July to August |
| 6 | [[Poṭṭhapāda]] | Rainy season | Tawthalin (တော်သလင်း) | Binara | August to September |
| 7 | [[Assayuja]] | Rainy season | Thadingyut (သီတင်းကျွတ်) | Vap | September to October |
| 8 | [[Kattikā]] | Rainy season | Tazaungmon (တန်ဆောင်မုန်း) | Il | October to November |
| 9 | [[Māgasira]] | Cold season | Nadaw (နတ်တော်) | Unduvap | November to December |
| 10 | [[Phussa]] | Cold season | Pyatho (ပြာသို) | Duruthu | December to January |
| 11 | [[Māgha]] | Cold season | Tabodwe (တပို့တွဲ) | Navam | January to February |
| 12 | [[Phagguṇa]] | Cold season | Tabaung (တပေါင်း) | Medin | February to March |
`});
